> [!WARNING]
> 
> **Material for MkDocs reaches end of life on May 5, 2027.** Critical
fixes and
> security updates continue until that date.
> 
> We're continuing our work with [Zensical], a 
> maintained successor built by the team behind Material for MkDocs. It
carries 
> forward what we've learned from building documentation tools with this
> community, with Markdown authoring, a familiar design, and full control
over 
> your content. Zensical is Open Source and MIT-licensed.
> 
> You can evaluate Zensical alongside MkDocs using your existing
`mkdocs.yml`.
> Check plugin compatibility and compare your pages, navigation, search,
and
> customizations before switching. The `classic` theme variant preserves
the
> appearance of Material for MkDocs. See the
> [migration guide]
> for the steps and current compatibility details.
> 
> [Upcoming changes on November 5]

## Quick start

Material for MkDocs requires Python 3.11 or newer. Install it with `pip`:

``` sh
pip install mkdocs-material
```

Add the following lines to `mkdocs.yml`:

``` yaml
theme:
  name: material
```

See the [installation guide]
for detailed instructions and the
[documentation]
for configuration options.

## Used by

Material for MkDocs has been used by projects including
[FastAPI],
[Pydantic],
[Ruff],
[OpenSSL],
[AWS Copilot], and
[Google Accompanist].

